1. License
   These Terms of Service are also the license agreement for Template. You are granted a non-exclusive,
   non-transferable license to install and use official releases of Template on Macs that you own or
   control. The software is licensed, not sold.

2. Free plan and Pro
   Template is free to use and the free plan includes every feature of the current release. If a paid Pro
   plan is offered, its features and price are shown on the website before you buy, and a Pro license covers
   every 1.x version.

3. License key
   A license key, where one is issued, is for the purchaser only and is active on a limited number of your
   own Macs at a time, stated at purchase. Do not transfer, rent, lend, share or resell it. To use it on
   another Mac, deactivate it on one of the others first.

4. Activation and verification
   The current release does not contact a licensing service. If a release adds license activation, it sends
   only the license key and a device label to Dodo Payments, and these terms say how often and how long Pro
   keeps working offline before that release ships.

5. Your data and credentials
   Template shows a list of items that it reads from a file in its own folder on your Mac
   (~/Library/Application Support). It does not read other files of yours, does not send the items anywhere
   and does not ask for any account or credential. If a future release stores a credential, it is kept in
   your Mac's keychain only.

6. Restrictions
   Without prior written permission of the copyright holder you may not: copy, modify, reverse engineer,
   decompile or disassemble the software (except where law expressly allows); redistribute, rent, lend,
   sublicense or sell it; bypass or tamper with license verification, where there is any; or remove copyright
   notices.

7. Updates
   Template checks for new versions once a day, and when you ask, by reading an update feed from
   dl.example.com. The request carries the app name and version, the update framework's version and, as with
   every web request, your IP address; no system profile is sent. A new version is installed only after you
   confirm, and Template installs it only if its signature is valid.

8. Third-party components
   Template includes Sparkle for updates. It is licensed separately (MIT License), not under this agreement.
   The list is in THIRD_PARTY.md.

9. Purchases and refunds
   Purchases are processed by Dodo Payments as the merchant of record, which calculates taxes for your
   region; Dodo's own terms apply to the payment. Refunds are covered by the Refund Policy
   (https://example.com/refund). This does not affect rights that the law gives you as a consumer.

10. Intellectual property
    The Template name, icon and software, and their copyright, belong to ydongy. Copyright (c) 2026
    ydongy. All rights reserved.

11. Termination
    If you breach these terms, your license ends automatically. If a license key stops working, for example
    after a refund, Template goes back to the free plan.

12. Disclaimer
    THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
    MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.

13. Limitation of liability
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the copyright holder is not liable for any indirect, incidental
    or consequential damages arising from use of the software, and the total liability is limited to the
    amount you paid for the license.

14. Changes
    These terms may be updated; the date above shows the latest version. If you keep using Template after an
    update, you accept it.

